                "quoted_status_profile_id": null,
                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 313,
                "retweet_count": 167,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "In an effort to advance President Trump\u2019s agenda, I voted \u201cPresent\u201d during tonight\u2019s Budget Committee markup to allow the legislation to move forward as we continue to improve it.\n\nWe\u2019ve made progress in negotiations, including moving work requirements for Medicaid forward, restricting future Green New Scam subsidies, and eliminating both the taxation and registration of suppressors under the NFA.\n\nYet there\u2019s still additional important work to be done to include as many America First priorities in President Trump\u2019s One Big Beautiful Bill as possible.\n\nI\u2019m fighting for key conservative wins\u2014including reducing deficit spending, fixing Medicaid to prioritize vulnerable Americans, slashing more Green New Scam subsidies, and restoring additional 2A constitutional rights.\n\nI will continue negotiating in good faith to improve this legislation before we pass the final product.\n\nThis is a rare opportunity to deliver real change for the American people. We can\u2014and must\u2014seize the moment.\n\nGiven the progress that we\u2019ve made, it\u2019s time for Republicans to be courageous.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
                "timestamp": 1747625656,
                "view_count": 36776
